 absence.\"},\"method\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Applicable task/sample/settings/metric and direct relevance or transfer limits.\"},\"comparability\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Material differences or missing fields and resulting comparison limits; mark not applicable when appropriate.\"},\"confidence\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Qualitative strength plus evidence-based reason, separate from status/provenance; no fabricated probabilities.\"},\"disposition\":{\"enum\":[\"retain\",\"qualify\",\"reject\",\"unknown\"],\"description\":\"Evidence disposition, provisional until Main checks support and method.\"}}}},\"gaps\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Named missing owned requirements, contradictions, access/budget limits and highest-impact resolving check.\"},\"stopReason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"Actual sufficient-support, diminishing-return, access, budget or blocked-conclusion reason. Budget stops are not evidence saturation.\"}}}}","status":"completed","runner":"pi","kernel":"typescript","transport":"process","cwd":"/home/balauru/.pi-profiles/fabric/.worktrees/research-skill-rework","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-terra","thinking":"high","startedAt":1788763245062,"updatedAt":1788763360025,"turns":5,"toolCalls":4,"text":"{\"assignment\":\"concurrency\",\"discovered\":[\"extensions.web_search\",\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"extensions.get_search_content\"],\"calls\":[{\"ref\":\"extensions.web_search\",\"args\":{\"queries\":[\"site:sqlite.org wal.html SQLite WAL concurrent writers readers same host network filesystem\",\"site:postgresql.org/docs current MVCC concurrent updates writers transaction isolation\",\"site:postgresql.org/docs current backup pg_basebackup online backup concurrent connections\"],\"numResults\":5,\"workflow\":\"none\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"3/3 queries successful; 15 total results.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvgvehtf27bc\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"args\":{\"urls\":[\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"https://www.sqlite.org/useovernet.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/mvcc-intro.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/transaction-iso.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-arch.html\"],\"mode\":\"readable\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"5/5 URLs fetched; 70,385 total extracted characters.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\",\"urlIndex\":0,\"findText\":[\"readers do not block writers\",\"only one writer at a time\",\"same host computer\"]},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"3 matching passages returned; no match for \\\"only one writer at a time\\\".\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\",\"urlIndex\":2,\"offset\":0,\"limit\":5000},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Complete PostgreSQL MVCC introduction returned, 1,612 characters.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\",\"urlIndex\":4,\"offset\":0,\"limit\":5000},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Complete PostgreSQL architecture section returned, 1,844 characters.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"}],\"rows\":[{\"id\":\"sqlite-reader-writer-overlap\",\"slot\":\"concurrency\",\"finding\":\"SQLite WAL documents concurrent reading and writing: readers do not block writers and a writer does not block readers.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"title\":\"Write-Ahead Logging\",\"passage\":\"WAL provides more concurrency as readers do not block writers and a writer does not block readers. Reading and writing can proceed concurrently.\",\"locator\":\"Advantages, introductory WAL section\",\"origin\":\"SQLite official documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"}],\"counterevidence\":\"The same retrieved page says this is \\\"mostly true\\\" and that some WAL-mode queries can return SQLITE_BUSY; applications should be prepared for that circumstance.\",\"method\":\"Applies when the database is operating in SQLite WAL mode. This is documented locking behavior, not a throughput measurement.\",\"comparability\":\"Directly comparable only to reader/writer overlap. It does not establish behavior for overlapping conflicting write transactions.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the stated reader/writer behavior because the exact current official WAL passage was retrieved.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"postgres-reader-writer-overlap\",\"slot\":\"concurrency\",\"finding\":\"PostgreSQL documents that MVCC read locks do not conflict with write locks, so reading never blocks writing and writing never blocks reading.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/mvcc-intro.html\",\"title\":\"13.1. Introduction\",\"passage\":\"The main advantage of using the MVCC model of concurrency control rather than locking is that in MVCC locks acquired for querying (reading) data do not conflict with locks acquired for writing data, and so reading never blocks writing and writing never blocks reading.\",\"locator\":\"MVCC introduction, paragraph 2\",\"origin\":\"PostgreSQL official documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"}],\"method\":\"Applies to PostgreSQL's documented MVCC behavior. This is not a measurement and does not define outcomes when writers contend for the same row.\",\"comparability\":\"Comparable to SQLite only for reader/writer overlap; write/write conflict handling was not extracted as an exact passage in this stream.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the stated reader/writer behavior because the exact current official MVCC passage was retrieved.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"sqlite-wal-deployment-boundary\",\"slot\":\"deployment\",\"finding\":\"SQLite WAL requires every process using the database to be on the same host; it does not work over a network filesystem.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"title\":\"Write-Ahead Logging\",\"passage\":\"All processes using a database must be on the same host computer; WAL does not work over a network filesystem. This is because WAL requires all processes to share a small amount of memory and processes on separate host machines obviously cannot share memory with each other.\",\"locator\":\"Disadvantages, introductory WAL section\",\"origin\":\"SQLite official documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"}],\"method\":\"Applies to SQLite in WAL mode where processes access the database directly.\",\"comparability\":\"This is a file-access deployment constraint, unlike PostgreSQL's client/server network interface.\",\"confidence\":\"High because the exact current official WAL limitation was retrieved.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"postgres-client-server-deployment\",\"slot\":\"deployment\",\"finding\":\"PostgreSQL documents a client/server model: server and client may be on different hosts over TCP/IP, and the server can handle multiple concurrent client connections.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-arch.html\",\"title\":\"1.2. Architectural Fundamentals\",\"passage\":\"As is typical of client/server applications, the client and the server can be on different hosts. In that case they communicate over a TCP/IP network connection.\",\"locator\":\"Architectural Fundamentals, client/server description\",\"origin\":\"PostgreSQL official documentation\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh49r38e0zl\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/tutorial-arch.html\",\"title\":\"1.2. Architectural Fundamentals\",\"passage\":\"The